" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668365} :answer-field/id #uuid "481b8271-af89-5177-b626-0e20a9c9d656" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05952a75-ee49-5c6e-985c-55f5554bd3f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-135311" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{bmatrix},\\,q=\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$q$ is a stochastic vector” is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement $Pq=q$ is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=\\begin{bmatrix}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.03+0.105+0.12 \\\\ 0.06+0.49+0.07 \\\\ 0.01+0.105+0.01\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.255 \\\\ 0.62 \\\\ 0.125\\end{bmatrix}\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$” is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$q$ is a stochastic vector” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef2a43dc-1c80-5218-8157-b47bfd63573e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/r