592186464280} :answer-field/id #uuid "793fa71c-2507-582d-aece-7b85ad9d5350" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00bbeb37-45cd-576b-a180-0506373ada19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668409} {:answer/id #uuid "f5973680-8186-5ba5-833d-cd1d4ca599de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5973680-8186-5ba5-833d-cd1d4ca599de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668410} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e2c0df5-4b3a-5a9c-a29c-15649ceb0f13" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e48e8cd-fab9-56d8-9673-3c5737feeff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143333" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=0.4.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.5\\cdot 0.6=0.3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=2,Y=2)\\ne P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e75e0302-d864-58b2-85e3-94ee824dd2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464282} {:answer/id #uuid "81aa670d-7b50-5dbc-876a-7211f2efdce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e75e0302-d864-58b2-85e3-94ee824dd2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464282} :answer-field/id #uuid "849d37e5-d949-564c-9ffb-269b4790643f" :answer-field/key "$P(X=0,Y=3)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a48738c-0702-53e5-be01-701b938eac9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464284} {:answer/id #uuid "ab470c08-52aa-55f5-9185-42801db2ff25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a48738c-0702-53e5-be01-701b938eac9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464284} :answer-field/id #uuid "0576c586-45c4-5fc2-ac45-e4e7ee3e0065" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc1e965d-3466-5f79-8631-71934ff94795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464286} {:answer/id #uuid "21ff56fe-204e-548f-804b-20588bc44e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc1e965d-3466-5f79-8631-71934ff94795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464286} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cb2efc-d508-5ae6-a259-fc9980908d16" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2612787-7130-5b72-af78-6a73372eded7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668411} {:answer/id #uuid "9238408d-76a1-51f0-9cab-de7e717b63fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9238408d-76a1-51f0-9cab-de7e717b63fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668412} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3b32732-8f46-5118-a803-5c75cce4f356" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16b71f57-df8c-5727-afc2-cdadae9185c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143334" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=0,Y=3)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=3)=f(0,3)=0.15.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3)=0.25\\cdot 0.3=0.075.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=3)\\ne P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7e9f64-cbbd-5bbd-8464-3f61b6f11586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464288} {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca347041-dadc-56e2-bbf1-f6ebc4c70e09" :answer-field/key "$P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} {:answer/id #uuid "006bf10f-88fe-5637-949f-4aa29407bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f7c971-351f-53ff-be7e-c7304f5c86bf" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a98f0c-64a9-57fe-b332-0fefcb246690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} :answer-field/id #uuid "da33b576-bcf0-5c09-83dd-58d6caaeb72b" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6eebeb-cdc2-5183-b1b0-4834ddafffd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668413} {:answer/id #uuid "902f7b21-a9f1-58ff-951e-8fd0a8f0c84f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6eebeb-cdc2-5183-b1b0-4834ddafffd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668413} :answer-field/id #uuid "025beb3e-6959-567f-9f0e-dc816967941e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "743eb09d-bf29-57ce-b05b-46da6dccd3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143338" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.8$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=3,Y=2)=f(3,2)=0.64.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.8\\cdot 0.8=0.64.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,2) & =0.16=0.2\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,4) & =0.01\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.1={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(4) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} {:answer/id #uuid "128d1ceb-39cf-5da3-8419-5a7d8a02044d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d189a29-6c25-5569-854b-c13fc0526360" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} {:answer/id #uuid "b3343df9-8a4a-5259-9ba0-3cd40ddbf9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} :answer-field/id #uuid "af0ced41-0208-507d-b83f-0b656205df0e" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0da6fb-3bb6-55a5-a319-72bfe95326c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee63d585-1abb-575b-b286-f0fc73957802" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9d1b1e8-170d-5cd8-a0a7-179202235004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668415} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcbb528-19dd-57f9-9e08-8b8dd39b3f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcbb528-19dd-57f9-9e08-8b8dd39b3f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668416} :answer-field/id #uuid "40113acf-b0b8-5beb-97b5-b23e717f19b0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d571385e-cc3b-5950-8471-24ba60f93b53" :question/math-academy-id "q-143435" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.05.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.3\\cdot 0.65=0.195.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=1,Y=1)\\ne P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity of Two-Piece Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c4716f3-6326-5ae4-bc45-acbb177ba3ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464372} {:answer/id #uuid "cae20107-711e-5689-a76e-614c066e0ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cae20107-711e-5689-a76e-614c066e0ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464373} :answer-field/id #uuid "3acf0d1a-c35b-588e-b935-587877be8fe8" :answer-field/key "$h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f52d418f-74c8-5a7e-84d8-1a6dc9a8f6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464374} {:answer/id #uuid "9c8c3919-ae46-507f-ace8-9d026c9df82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f52d418f-74c8-5a7e-84d8-1a6dc9a8f6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464374} :answer-field/id #uuid "01699db0-6d10-5984-be18-d09dc01a0e3a" :answer-field/key "$h(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e35c5396-bc57-56ec-b1cb-5d29be77cca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464376} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4175ec-8ee3-5e23-b5c1-462cd6cef567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e35c5396-bc57-56ec-b1cb-5d29be77cca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464376} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad7f5c7-8b54-5d58-ac2b-8482656e163d" :answer-field/key "$h(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35060dab-e395-567d-90cd-ae29a625d395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668417} {:answer/id #uuid "9710f7f5-ea89-5b80-bf22-846985feb9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35060dab-e395-567d-90cd-ae29a625d395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668417} :answer-field/id #uuid "689caa68-4ddb-5441-bc17-616d87d59e39" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a65475e2-5e0e-5ab6-8415-f174e9dcfcbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-149751" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $h(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nh(x)={\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{-x}, & x\\le -1 \\\\ 1-2x, & x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x=-1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $h(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-1) & =-\\sqrt{-(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1$” is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}h(x) & =-\\sqrt{-(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =h(-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$h(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function is *not* right-continuous at $x=-1$ since the right-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}h(x) & =1-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3 \\\\  & \\ne h(-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$h(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$” is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b5963fe-823f-5433-b587-0ff85bf05ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464378} {:answer/id #uuid "e5805653-1c99-5ce4-a1b2-2f3abbf31dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5805653-1c99-5ce4-a1b2-2f3abbf31dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464379} :answer-field/id #uuid "6992528f-7f94-56b5-8ebf-72131f3f9f66" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592