ckbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdbd7939-21af-5d98-9fc2-2a05d548f266" :question/math-academy-id "q-149832" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{3}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{3}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d1f5b74-5fdc-5c2f-910a-09a005af8e81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464396} {:answer/id #uuid "175316c7-1adf-5b8d-9638-61dd2beadeec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "175316c7-1adf-5b8d-9638-61dd2beadeec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464397} :answer-field/id #uuid "689c5fa5-ba6c-5e0d-a930-75571a26cf6e" :answer-field/key "$EF=FE={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac1e17b4-aee8-5fc5-8886-0a6cc9af81d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464398} {:answer/id #uuid "80fd3428-c192-5980-99ad-b767ce6f34a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac1e17b4-aee8-5fc5-8886-0a6cc9af81d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464398} :answer-field/id #uuid "9360b20c-7cda-5648-84a2-06445bc9ec4a" :answer-field/key "$FG=GF={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a03919-ca84-5fcc-84b3-a6150ed38402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464400} {:answer/id #uuid "812754e6-e6a9-505c-b216-977872b3454c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57a03919-ca84-5fcc-84b3-a6150ed38402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464400} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e458fe-d597-518a-9c37-c84225521501" :answer-field/key "$F={G}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8790c3ca-8ba3-5ff0-9657-d95bfd2508ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668425} {:answer/id #uuid "8e3bf888-f75b-583a-a59b-8e58411fb545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8790c3ca-8ba3-5ff0-9657-d95bfd2508ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668425} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cebe1fd-11a0-530c-8073-598425788313" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e4c02d8-0c31-5630-b78b-ca07d9d8a348" :question/math-academy-id "q-149833" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,G=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $EF=FE={I}_{3}.$ Computing $EF$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $FE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FE & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $EF=FE={I}_{3}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $FG=GF={I}_{3}.$ Computing $FG$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FG & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $FG=GF={I}_{3}$ is false. As a result, $F\\ne {G}^{-1}$ and statement $F={G}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $EF=FE={I}_{3}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity at a Point Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25dd7c3c-5e1d-5f4b-8a27-458746ccd605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464430} {:answer/id #uuid "00c2746a-be60-54e6-8f79-587f24bb51b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00c2746a-be60-54e6-8f79-587f24bb51b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464431} :answer-field/id #uuid "e533970f-a7ba-508a-922c-164e8ef8f9c4" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bcef6b3-734d-5f3b-b9b4-3f1df1d84661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464432} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbfe0e8-324d-5440-a9e0-aea861f8fcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fbfe0e8-324d-5440-a9e0-aea861f8fcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464433} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e928c5b-21bf-5add-b0b5-cda5e2f4e753" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0abea3d-fbd5-5b7d-985e-4f1321fad0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464434} {:answer/id #uuid "37cea012-ac20-558c-9b6c-79754347401b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37cea012-ac20-558c-9b6c-79754347401b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464435} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ca9507d-09f0-5602-b837-c46983484bd7" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d54fd92-3963-580f-8ce6-e267e8c2283e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464436} {:answer/id #uuid "5085f31b-5c7c-5afe-9ea5-2b9dff9780a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d54fd92-3963-580f-8ce6-e267e8c2283e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464436} :answer-field/id #uuid "4909e442-e10e-5268-96f3-76d3ff27ca3e" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5c5c03e-1fc4-58de-bc92-f496767b8974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668427} {:answer/id #uuid "916b3358-046e-5cb3-b772-3312abdcf4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c5c03e-1fc4-58de-bc92-f496767b8974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668427} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fa58d5-e251-5b58-a161-7e37fe6e7d6e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22700976-ee21-5930-ae8c-a7e530babcbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-152930" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-4-x, & x\\le 2 \\\\ -3x, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$” is true. Using the expression for the first branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(2)=-4-2=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)$ is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(-4-x) \\\\  & =-4-2 \\\\  & =-6 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(-3x) \\\\  & =-3(2) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=f(2)$ is true. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6=f(2).$  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$” is false. Since all statements “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$”; ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)$; ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=f(2)$ are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$”; ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)$; ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=f(2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83796fe8-f045-5dbc-94d1-6d6e031f3ed8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Line Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:an