c-3a1b-5878-baac-a4471022f29c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ecd1a30-d61f-5d31-96d2-62fa52545c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158029" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram I is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace.  In this case, we have that the vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398c4cf2-b5b9-558d-832b-37f666218d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465297} {:answer/id #uuid "412b77ef-dc77-580c-befa-7e9379a921e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "412b77ef-dc77-580c-befa-7e9379a921e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465298} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a10b74b-d355-5da6-b34a-57def74627a4" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8526823d-abcc-54bf-8af4-da58bb047c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465299} {:answer/id #uuid "aec99e2a-8eb4-58b4-9590-18a02351b254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8526823d-abcc-54bf-8af4-da58bb047c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465299} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e8b78d8-7d38-52f4-ad95-3cc927aa6e15" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901b8d79-bea7-584b-99ca-ebc77ca52742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465301} {:answer/id #uuid "bcdc5504-5f38-536f-9b87-1ee4610cde1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901b8d79-bea7-584b-99ca-ebc77ca52742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465301} :answer-field/id #uuid "1622fd27-1eaf-55b1-b8a8-b142061f2303" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b313ac-804c-5358-bce6-12efb3434cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668437} {:answer/id #uuid "c24237e0-b187-5f44-b739-bca263c01fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21b313ac-804c-5358-bce6-12efb3434cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668437} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8d0639-b9ab-5d04-9256-ef33f552c7b3" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b24e08c4-4299-5d2f-a3af-dcce0689b7c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-160447" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x/2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{x/2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x/2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & =2({e}^{0}-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8574032e-7d34-5165-a4e0-00628f417667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465303} {:answer/id #uuid "7c831406-c2c1-5a56-b6e8-99b724d7c7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c831406-c2c1-5a56-b6e8-99b724d7c7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465304} :answer-field/id #uuid "b968f63e-b65b-5762-920c-5c39cf8c5680" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d474bfd9-08af-50f8-a009-ffd1c5fa29a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465305} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9e254d-304a-5fcb-ba2e-abddfc9762b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d474bfd9-08af-50f8-a009-ffd1c5fa29a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465305} :answer-field/id #uuid "580e15f7-7c9b-5b5b-b207-504cf71ede08" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60289d96-5d64-506a-bb60-39aea93ffe10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465307} {:answer/id #uuid "cc49bedf-8d39-5a9a-b0c5-310023c19458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60289d96-5d64-506a-bb60-39aea93ffe10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b0fc18-cd28-52cf-a80e-e991e6040ca2" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbb51bdd-eba8-5d04-8d09-d312debc8538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668439} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2761bc-fd5e-5e6b-911e-91bc7db269c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb51bdd-eba8-5d04-8d09-d312debc8538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668439} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc6de2a-025d-509d-a5e3-55ab5e6dfaff" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0b61c31-2e3e-5b9a-9684-a3b763cdba2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-160450" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3afe07d2-ac9e-5cf3-a0df-a60fba1947a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465309} {:answer/id #uuid "39b9a9e2-b274-59d1-a806-fb760cfa292c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39b9a9e2-b274-59d1-a806-fb760cfa292c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465310} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7a9fb37-814f-59d8-98df-cf807c43024a" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "785644ac-003f-5ff6-bd02-b0063c3522f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465311} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e4e5d1-4b09-51f4-9dc6-03ca0eac53c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "785644ac-003f-5ff6-bd02-b0063c3522f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465311} :answer-field/id #uuid "7670715a-8a93-5131-b8d0-47fc4afd8030" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4cbbe22-5b0a-5c75-9b19-864b6a6135d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465313} {:answer/id #uuid "37c1c95c-f41d-553a-a794-3684167e0740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4cbbe22-5b0a-5c75-9b19-864b6a6135d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465313} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7db66c4-37dd-5377-b424-3bc72a80a6f1" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466500} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dd53859-7da4-50c9-a796-9e31adaad703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668441} {:answer/id #uuid "1a05b60a-3639-58ff-8462-780c0b8d8ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd53859-7da4-50c9-a796-9e31adaad703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668441} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3f1551-ea24-5b8f-a7a9-e74d1c590ea9" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9f1f757-0f29-5257-92da-0c605e690da7" :question/math-academy-id "q-160455" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{1-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=2{e}^{1-2x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Horizontal Segment Under a Polar Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e9d7f9d-83aa-5312-b9f9-936431142ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465369} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac8bfb2-2b9e-55b8-bb40-8f8acd30ba03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9d7f9d-83aa-5312-b9f9-936431142ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465369} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c3a02a3-a8fc-5d7d-a6a6-ce9f21391422" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7781f3c-7002-5af8-8927-9ec981d328c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465371} {:answer/id #uuid "a99cc1de-6948-5f01-b0c0-9f08fcb47a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a99cc1de-6948-5f01-b0c0-9f08fcb47a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465372} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb1bd5d-92e5-55ab-9836-46ae0a7485ce" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7401365f-e9ac-59db-a5a4-772ee4d7ef48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465373} {:answer/id #uuid "cd23ead9-89df-5865-9f9e-b85c6d699f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7401365f-e9ac-59db-a5a4-772ee4d7ef48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465373} :answer-field/id #uuid "789e9739-d69d-5715-b272-2c686ab19b73" :answer-field/key "One endpoint of the image is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, and the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $5$ centered at $O.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466530} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d524e1c8-75bd-54de-9e22-2ce3bec030c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668443} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e1cb80-bbd8-5798-a57c-def4ea6a6f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d524e1c8-75bd-54de-9e22-2ce3bec030c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668443} :answer-field/id #uuid "f69b48c0-599a-5f48-a455-b2a39ef17646" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35901d5d-b737-59bd-bd22-20c686ac3fe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161035" :question/problem "![](images/8a/8afe0884ccf1e62ffdfef6cab4626bc59b3138aa5cd26f855980c88971753447.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/b8/b836799bc512db70d2ce5fcfe70db2af3b2572d584d317fa5ed515b363a11ddc.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis” is false, while statement “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis” is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement “One endpoint of the image is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, and the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $5$ centered at $O.$” is false.\n\n- When $u=0,$ we obtain the point $(0,\\,0),$ which is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane.\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{5},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right),\\,\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)),$\nwhose distance to $O$ is $\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo, one endpoint of the segment is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, while the other endpoint lies in the circle with radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a5de68-5950-514f-9ba1-08fa9d4299ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465387} {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb986ee-74d8-55e7-ace6-4c46cc82d2fa" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc276e3-6d65-585e-9956-fe2637e49b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} :answer-field/id #uuid "845a991c-16c1-5dca-bbbc-d4f135e22f63" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=2-y-z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} {:answer/id #uuid "328852b4-a1a4-578a-9f26-a0109eec8aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14d9582-0fba-5cac-a562-27db433f61d6" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=2+y-z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49097e2d-5786-54a6-b743-30b38fe4a2d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668445} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a04e6c-4cec-5827-bfcf-f3fc466f9445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49097e2d-5786-54a6-b743-30b38fe4a2d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668445} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b4b61f0-f02d-5cb8-bb9d-b8057f467f9d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83e332b2-7a45-565f-946e-09fe8f179dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161247" :question/problem "![](images/60/60f622b161dbfb4da1d18e85d3eb3ab4e02c2af418f9845e05a3bf9704a28006.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $x=0,$ and $x=2+y-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statements “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=2-y-z$” and “${f}_{1}(y,z)=2+y-z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=5$” are false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=2+y-z.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2af4029bd979d250ed15f351ef7f14d3ae688806db4ffec199a24b3591dadac.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dea8612-414c-5394-869d-1e404b048156" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type III Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87947aba-3ee6-5f0b-b3c6-cd6a066bd244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465399} {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5ae30f-59ec-58d7-a15c-4249798540d9" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ca98d-56b9-5e97-bfb2-dff3175e39ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} :answer-field/id #uuid "73340b15-0013-5823-988c-a3ba50461d3c" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=z-\\frac{x}{3}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eae65db7-54ff-596a-b1e0-2327b0ecaba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465403} {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb2eb83-9dd5-5fd0-a343-cff27dd76ab1" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d965a0f-fc64-5614-bc9f-6737ae9ec597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668447} {:answer/id #uuid "efa2da36-7703-557e-bbe1-d2729a261c12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d965a0f-fc64-5614-bc9f-6737ae9ec597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668447} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2698503-12af-5c01-8734-55ebd24e3b21" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bbc7b8c-0af0-5315-ba58-db2c9cd43206" :question/math-academy-id "q-161250" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d447e5a00aa324d83a3f513db11ff677fd2db2c7b1b33d8bc2bcfa73b4a08f3f.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $y=0,$ and $y=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {f}_{2}(x,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type III region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3333ded3e00e7d7408f0dbd37807f1adec0301691cc6311871bfea6d7b9fa15.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=z-\\frac{x}{3}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3$” is false, while statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$” is true. We have\n\n- the *left* surface $y={f}_{1}(x,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *right* surface $y={f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$\n\n![](images/88/88b5fde383f094436dd94adefa7912f1a194319739fdb0b8a6a9a74693362219.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057db65a-eecb-52c7-ac69-c8a69baf0264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465405} {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4918c6-67e4-5f19-84fb-a1e03896cf0d" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c8e774-2be1-50a4-be88-195ee7a64ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465407} {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408} :answer-field/id #uuid "bed649e4-9512-5df5-8690-508a27d9b3e5" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} {:answer/id #uuid "b1856245-617f-5aa9-b2a6-f6ea110eeb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} :answer-field/id #uuid "c51647d3-edd0-55aa-b2d7-68154b9214d2" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=4+y-2z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a77ae8e-76a0-548d-910c-b37e90e89e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668449} {:answer/id #uuid "b008d616-08d8-5a92-b0ef-f2c1ca49663c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a77ae8e-76a0-548d-910c-b37e90e89e77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668449} :answer-field/id #uuid "8424b719-fad2-5eb2-b3b8-996aa6d05d41" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f1a985-1f99-5d8b-a66e-0643cac8da20" :question/math-academy-id "q-161361" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7799ca5801bf019fc5b884590575346a8f298f8e9c91056c13a60c4dd23742d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=3$, $x=0,$ and $x=4-y+2z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$” is true and statement “${f}_{1}(y,z)=4+y-2z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4$” is false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z.$\n\n![](images/3b/3bf8e141067fb6f675933f52e465114d8909d951f6ac85fb09c8dda7efbc2f38.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "769ab244-b50f-5cca-ab22-fd43c9447cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465411} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5149c3-ecba-57d2-b462-3dbdfb69933a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "769ab244-b50f-5cca-ab22-fd43c9447cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465411} :answer-field/id #uuid "087f9ca1-8165-5d08-815b-de98c18b98c3" :answer-field/key "$A$ contains none of its boundary points." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61780875-68b1-505b-895f-12ff1ff66c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465413} {:answer/id #uuid "dad38122-7c39-50f3-9242-6e99cb69a4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61780875-68b1-505b-895f-12ff1ff66c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465413} :answer-field/id #uuid "65372a61-77ce-559a-9860-6323bcc95b27" :answer-field/key "$A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0696dc0-2a39-515e-89a4-41b079d76ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465415} {:answer/id #uuid "61f6634a-9066-5bbf-b0fc-703e680d6c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61f6634a-9066-5bbf-b0fc-703e680d6c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465416} :answer-field/id #uuid "db274c98-e65f-53ec-bc5e-861c8411a39d" :answer-field/key "$\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d368d45-b048-5dc2-8e28-71002f972f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668451} {:answer/id #uuid "1783ccfa-2d53-5813-942c-d6dd8da45f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d368d45-b048-5dc2-8e28-71002f972f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668451} :answer-field/id #uuid "11c7695c-a4e0-58c1-b42c-67b87a877fb6" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be0484aa-ac87-5330-9ede-cd54e1386a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-161625" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cdca164d343d8bff4c78a1e366e52c588ca6c54dfdea61acea1900bcbdc79f31.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements “$A$ contains none of its boundary points” and “$A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points” are false. As we have seen, $A$ contains all its boundary points.\n\n- Statement $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$ is true. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f3745d-f09c-5360-a931-21a667dd1d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465453} {:answer/id #uuid "21ed980e-4000-5687-a17b-d84e6f1e4479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ed980e-4000-5687-a17b-d84e6f1e4479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465454} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8bbd34-591c-5d0f-b655-42fc58838887" :answer-field/key "$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "835fd9d2-ac5f-5fc7-a341-f53a230e3899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465455} {:answer/id #uuid "1205f76c-8469-5ede-a981-4f167eb37530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "835fd9d2-ac5f-5fc7-a341-f53a230e3899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465455} :answer-field/id #uuid "d92c5843-42f4-52a3-a501-b15764eb3a62" :answer-field/key "${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36cd71c2-430d-5fd7-a358-b102308c8d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465457} {:answer/id #uuid "71481a29-9e86-5894-95fe-7fecf6d21f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36cd71c2-430d-5fd7-a358-b102308c8d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465457} :answer-field/id #uuid "a98b628c-ca32-5dd8-8891-b556d9bd4149" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=2.91$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9d67f5-20e0-5e21-a6ae-75000bf9cc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668453} {:answer/id #uuid "74516797-d713-56d7-a7b6-ba3702932349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b9d67f5-20e0-5e21-a6ae-75000bf9cc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668453} :answer-field/id #uuid "384f2eb7-9f05-56b7-90fb-9d9569953cfc" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4eb620b0-5fb5-5c19-a1ea-9934c615ac57" :question/math-academy-id "q-161857" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a79260df29825684d6bdf6197df8581adf5a5a2d1d89938c299f18b3f33bf7c.png)\n\nThe function $f(x),$ whose graph is shown above, has a stationary point at $x=2$ and is continuously differentiable everywhere except at $x=3.$  By considering the points indicated in the diagram, determine which of the following statements **must** be true according to the inverse function theorem.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$” is true. The function $f$ satisfies the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=1.$ Indeed,\n\n- $f$ is continuously differentiable on an open set containing $x=1,$ for example, $(0,2),$ and\n\n- the derivative of $f$ is nonzero at $x=1,$ i.e., ${f}^{′}(1)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, by the inverse function theorem, $f$ is invertible in *some* neighborhood of $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=-2$” is false. Notice that $y=-2=f(2).$  However, the function $f$ does *not* satisfy the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=2$ since ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=2.91$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)}$” is false. Notice that $y=2.91=f(3),$ but $f$ is not continuous at $x=3.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1257faba-9e7b-5cca-8ae5-84b10e9a9aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465459} {:answer/id #uuid "38ddbd87-a974-5584-bfba-bd3e8c19432d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1257faba-9e7b-5cca-8ae5-84b10e9a9aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465459} :answer-field/id #uuid "41153c5d-1a60-56f9-9889-e3734c88b5fc" :answer-field/key "$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466573} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57884e71-d5eb-506d-a128-dafffc6cb068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465461} {:answer/id #uuid "20be9fdc-8871-57ef-a9b8-8c9a211d7e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57884e71-d5eb-506d-a128-dafffc6cb068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465461} :answer-field/id #uuid "73e0fc32-e0b5-5737-beea-a8d93563b24b" :answer-field/key "${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d127b5a-2c09-5d77-b9cd-0489463d1715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465463} {:answer/id #uuid "9deb9bc4-9347-59f4-82b8-fc109454910a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9deb9bc4-9347-59f4-82b8-fc109454910a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465464} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ddba5e6-8fb0-518c-b7d8-7cac2d5ca0ba" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=4$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c11bba9-6cb3-5d90-8ca8-df54e8f4a76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668455} {:answer/id #uuid "ef29a114-64f1-5988-9959-91ab37ad6663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c11bba9-6cb3-5d90-8ca8-df54e8f4a76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668455} :answer-field/id #uuid "864cbdbd-ba92-5980-a340-896726811b9d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "649157e5-32cb-5583-98fc-af0b21c39379" :question/math-academy-id "q-161858" :question/problem "![](images/54/540e1fac13ed45d6db5c857678a7ccf410b3834213adb2b984cb6f942d4dba2f.png)\n\nThe function $f(x),$ whose graph is shown above, has a stationary point at $x=-2$ and is continuously differentiable everywhere except at $x=-3.$  By considering the points indicated in the diagram, determine which of the following statements **must** be true according to the inverse function theorem.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=-3$” is false. Notice that $f$ is not continuous at $x=-3.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=2$” is also false. Notice that $y=2=f(-2).$  However, the function $f$ does *not* satisfy the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=-2$ since ${f}^{′}(-2)=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=4$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)}$” is true. Notice that $y=4=f(0),$ and the function $f$ satisfies the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=0.$ Indeed,\n\n- $f$ is continuously differentiable on an open set containing $x=0,$ for example, $(-0.1,0.1),$ and\n\n- the derivative of $f$ is nonzero at $x=0,$ i.e., ${f}^{′}(0)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, by the inverse function theorem, the derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=4$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=4$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6482623d-8c4e-5651-a72b-e7411d79d809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465465} {:answer/id #uuid "939961c0-1305-54a9-818b-09cfc0d38502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "939961c0-1305-54a9-818b-09cfc0d38502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465466} :answer-field/id #uuid "82301762-7b0f-595d-b514-4ced579d9cbf" :answer-field/key "$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6687532f-6a13-5099-9722-b86b313bd075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465467} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5ff3f4-5cfd-5289-a27a-38a8b986e0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6687532f-6a13-5099-9722-b86b313bd075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465467} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b945cf-8f03-5126-b845-2288e60189d1" :answer-field/key "${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=-0.88$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8985717d-57ba-54c8-9bc4-d11aee23fe95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465469} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a7dd18-8d8e-5642-834e-a057e86e24aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8985717d-57ba-54c8-9bc4-d11aee23fe95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465469} :answer-field/id #uuid "e731320a-3d91-5595-9f7e-2db38ae1357f" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=2.5$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78143eb9-ae65-5a43-81c4-ca032f1544bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668457} {:answer/id #uuid "a2123028-21d1-5753-8475-8f3a464d5a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78143eb9-ae65-5a43-81c4-ca032f1544bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668457} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5859a1-1340-505f-bf4c-a71adfb0e529" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c687527-ddc3-50e7-9a3f-531649897edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161865" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa872c37fc7912e4c246c80c391ee37ae57f23f6c1010681c367ce2ec6d901c2.png)\n\nThe function $f(x),$ whose graph is shown above, has a stationary point at $x=3$ and is continuously differentiable everywhere except at $x=0.$  By considering the points indicated in the diagram, determine which of the following statements **must** be true according to the inverse function theorem.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$” is true. The function $f$ satisfies the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=1.$ Indeed,\n\n- $f$ is continuously differentiable on an open set containing $x=1,$ for example, $(0.5,1.5),$ and\n\n- the derivative of $f$ is nonzero at $x=1,$ i.e., ${f}^{′}(1)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, by the inverse function theorem, $f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “${f}^{-1}(y)$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $y=-0.88$” is false. Notice that $y=-0.88=f(0),$ but $f$ is not continuous at $x=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}(y)$ at $y=2.5$ equals $\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)}$” is also false. Notice that $y=2.5=f(3).$  However, the function $f$ does *not* satisfy the conditions for the inverse function theorem at $x=3$ since ${f}^{′}(3)=0.$ So, the theorem can't be applied in this situation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $x=1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc10e234-82ec-548f-b508-b8a34d60de48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465477} {:answer/id #uuid "19cc9d63-26ae-5d67-8d2e-92a25b620c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19cc9d63-26ae-5d67-8d2e-92a25b620c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465478} :answer-field/id #uuid "76684f2a-492a-5359-ab60-ed33c7131dda" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d585690c-260f-5e71-a6e3-572e7e3486d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465479} {:answer/id #uuid "2dfff1c9-8854-533f-bcbe-5d8a3b55044b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d585690c-260f-5e71-a6e3-572e7e3486d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465479} :answer-field/id #uuid "d16a6f9f-f813-5bc0-8804-79ea114f5d79" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "934f59a6-e3f6-570b-9a54-e524e4c540a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465481} {:answer/id #uuid "abb738ed-ecd8-58af-9c55-39b58795284c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "934f59a6-e3f6-570b-9a54-e524e4c540a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465481} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec28cbc6-2271-5aa3-a1c8-3a8a32cf506a" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1884105b-2016-5b30-bd51-cea36cfaec9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668459} {:answer/id #uuid "41196774-ca8d-5f6b-aecd-23be94dc23dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1884105b-2016-5b30-bd51-cea36cfaec9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668459} :answer-field/id #uuid "e95beaeb-e4cb-500d-b44e-97c8b73043f9" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5dd282b-2dab-5297-89c3-a4849921b265" :question/math-academy-id "q-162746" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.06$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.24$ | $0.06$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |  |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.06.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.2\\cdot 0.3=0.06.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0) & =0.1\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b6d959-ee25-5492-981c-35d8db8e5d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465483} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9adef5-225c-5e47-85de-42b3cd7836b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b6d959-ee25-5492-981c-35d8db8e5d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465483} :answer-field/id #uuid "14307e24-b8d0-5de1-9104-6c06ac0c93ca" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=0)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "655fd2b1-caba-581e-9f02-5af690a77b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465485} {:answer/id #uuid "68af336e-64bf-56bf-84dd-85cd858cec6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655fd2b1-caba-581e-9f02-5af690a77b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465485} :answer-field/id #uuid "d37345fc-3288-5bfa-8a83-9ad74cabae6f" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f3db53-a644-5ca7-a50d-da78184c6ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465487} {:answer/id #uuid "10595161-cfd2-59f2-802a-94f7478661b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7f3db53-a644-5ca7-a50d-da78184c6ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465487} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf4bd53-b362-55cb-86c6-31f5ad34dba8" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee2f724-48e5-5863-a7b3-37b8497007e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668461} {:answer/id #uuid "d84752b5-d7ed-5ec2-823a-b4d62556be3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d84752b5-d7ed-5ec2-823a-b4d62556be3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668462} :answer-field/id #uuid "533c65e1-d90d-512a-ad71-0dd369d7bad9" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "745e2846-c808-51fa-a431-23f636897e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-162824" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.5$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=1,Y=0)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=0)=f(1,0)=0.25.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0)=0.5\\cdot 0.6=0.3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=1,Y=0)\\ne P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=0),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6bd5f7b-86e2-5e7e-b73c-315158951242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465489} {:answer/id #uuid "69898b06-6833-5e82-bda7-be2ba91dcd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69898b06-6833-5e82-bda7-be2ba91dcd05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465490} :answer-field/id #uuid "64426418-f534-5933-9f46-35719ecf03ce" :answer-field/key "$P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dece8f5a-d33c-55b1-8727-78b35148f159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465491} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0e11ca-3eba-54ba-b933-6364f809561b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a0e11ca-3eba-54ba-b933-6364f809561b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465492} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a934dbd-cdc8-57f7-8678-a94b82ca59cf" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11b7752-cf12-5634-a8c7-a28b035c3ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465493} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8854e9-a444-5ea2-b47b-67f40c37002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8854e9-a444-5ea2-b47b-67f40c37002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465494} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ef4a0e-65a8-501a-9a5a-8c9657c7647e" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe72a28a-79c1-50f9-8e2f-e04f62581599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668463} {:answer/id #uuid "2dffae7f-ff18-5d4b-8c20-d5cae897c9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe72a28a-79c1-50f9-8e2f-e04f62581599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668463} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6eb454-04f1-5bd2-83bd-cf6629ce6e1d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24b5d8-591a-5107-953f-3194f9f2c074" :question/math-academy-id "q-163605" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{12}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{24}$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{3}{8}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{8}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=-2)=f(0,-2)=\\frac{1}{4}.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =\\frac{5}{12}=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,-2) & =\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,2) & =\\frac{5}{24}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=0,Y=-2)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de7257-8d35-5f81-89be-c7faa73d6bc3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a8ad20-3764-5670-8078-71b7721fc577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465495} {:answer/id #uuid "27b99241-25ca-5909-922e-fe366e5d4927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27b99241-25ca-5909-922e-fe366e5d4927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465496} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa1944d-ce09-51f9-8a91-e6875021ae04" :answer-field/key "$P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4f6faf-e175-54c4-a961-1ff23aedd8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465497} {:answer/id #uuid "057dab26-bc3c-5bcc-81b6-1a2bb82c5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "057dab26-bc3c-5bcc-81b6-1a2bb82c5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465498} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e7a4211-9bc2-523c-9177-898dbab2152d" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d6ce853-4f78-5f21-87d1-1b375cb77cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465499} {:answer/id #uuid "0da85821-e95e-5859-8a01-ba978cb19b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da85821-e95e-5859-8a01-ba978cb19b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465500} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a10f283-8c48-5c9d-a0f4-a9c8b4e9c55e" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466593} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59b85f2-2464-5af9-afdf-95d924ca18e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668465} {:answer/id #uuid "01fe9171-69d9-5543-b5ca-060b1b7d3777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59b85f2-2464-5af9-afdf-95d924ca18e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668465} :answer-field/id #uuid "778210c3-f508-5ca6-88ec-4afabb233182" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25bf9bc6-630d-50c0-9382-20c9fae3e81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163617" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $0.22$ | $0.33$ |\n| $X=8$ | $0.18$ | $0.27$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | |  | | $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=8,Y=1)=f(8,1)=0.27.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(8)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.45\\cdot 0.6=0.27.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =0.22=0.55\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-1) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,1) & =0.33=0.55\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(8,-1) & =0.18=0.45\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(8)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-1) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=8,Y=1)$ $=P(X=8)\\cdot P(Y=1)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb319d62-cd43-5416-b0dd-4e83919c9d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465501} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb461ff-be99-576b-bd61-91dd215bc98d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb319d62-cd43-5416-b0dd-4e83919c9d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465501} :answer-field/id #uuid "34ad56ac-7ece-5f66-8726-bc1880a95996" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=5$ and $det(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79f8c24-9355-5076-90c6-a4367316d750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465503} {:answer/id #uuid "0f345692-7fb4-5ba8-be20-f1cb86aeca50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f345692-7fb4-5ba8-be20-f1cb86aeca50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c07de42-afc1-558c-98b8-9dbe9fa265a9" :answer-field/key "$A$ is positive-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad342ee-39e5-5988-818a-6cf740e323a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465505} {:answer/id #uuid "61e4a967-940f-553b-b00f-ad2e376fcd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61e4a967-940f-553b-b00f-ad2e376fcd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465506} :answer-field/id #uuid "66e05cae-0986-5eea-b30c-263f052d000a" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176421a6-fe88-5aee-94c6-bf927e037529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668467} {:answer/id #uuid "daf65277-30a7-55ed-a28f-2c0eac0fe806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "176421a6-fe88-5aee-94c6-bf927e037529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668467} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa091a57-22dd-542d-b0d2-15fc21823e97" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59d86f24-1bbb-55d7-8154-a7330272c0b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163779" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈4+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=5$ and $det(A)=2$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=5,$ but\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is positive-definite” is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=5>0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is positive-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local minimum of $f$” is true. Since the matrix $A$ is positive-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local minimum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is positive-definite”; “$a$ is a local minimum of $f$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35364fce-dfa4-57e3-b4b3-7ffde26baef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465507} {:answer/id #uuid "abe81707-7bee-5f3d-9998-a89d0e5199e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35364fce-dfa4-57e3-b4b3-7ffde26baef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465507} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40580c0-664c-5c83-92d6-b7ba6d5f88f8" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c4f5088-9b18-50ac-a385-00e43fa6bfd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465509} {:answer/id #uuid "30bdc7e6-fb2d-5f8e-8626-9b6d3ba37448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30bdc7e6-fb2d-5f8e-8626-9b6d3ba37448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465510} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4dbc50-2382-5ace-b738-59f70f7581ec" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35500f5f-9589-57c1-b99a-e40289eb9def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465511} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbd6160-5664-504d-af50-fadc01831e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35500f5f-9589-57c1-b99a-e40289eb9def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465511} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb722114-368c-5b3a-8c4c-b807849699e9" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8e34aba-b782-57dd-865f-8d8dbc2d18bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668469} {:answer/id #uuid "16d96e96-fe19-533c-9f2d-f69f99d58c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8e34aba-b782-57dd-865f-8d8dbc2d18bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668469} :answer-field/id #uuid "be401d20-a82e-5719-988f-f54823a964bf" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03651691-7356-5261-96f0-0d0badb00da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163780" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈-8+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, let's recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=-1$ and $det(A)=4$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-1,$ but\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}|=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-1<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}|=2>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local minimum of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is negative-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e792ff8-af62-57d5-a566-a450e4d2c073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465513} {:answer/id #uuid "c06e501a-7fca-57b5-8fd8-00c7ba0828ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e792ff8-af62-57d5-a566-a450e4d2c073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465513} :answer-field/id #uuid "7767a756-a8d3-5be5-bfc9-c38d9f8739ab" :answer-field/key "${a}_{11}=3$ and $det(A)>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d91f22ee-b903-5aa9-a3a0-e9971360e020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465515} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaa9832-b748-5975-984c-dd66a942f7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddaa9832-b748-5975-984c-dd66a942f7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465516} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa63e50-d620-5761-8485-c5faf4821dd9" :answer-field/key "$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476a495d-1c2e-59e7-a3f1-54bf4179f4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465517} {:answer/id #uuid "6a781903-27e5-5a45-afd1-4d6f7a5fdce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a781903-27e5-5a45-afd1-4d6f7a5fdce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465518} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b937cb6-cf67-521a-8508-427cc88aed42" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a saddle point of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d661981-7ef6-547f-8559-ebc1a2e52f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668471} {:answer/id #uuid "28d0287c-1fe7-58c2-ae53-e5d4f2d2915d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d661981-7ef6-547f-8559-ebc1a2e52f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668471} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7966b7-90b2-5399-8401-a776cbc48f54" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c598e2d2-d26a-59ea-a0e5-a7e53e350ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163789" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈16+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${a}_{11}=3$ and $det(A)>0$” is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=3,$ but\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3)-1(-2)-4(7) \\\\  & =-17<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite” is true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=3>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=5>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-17<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a saddle point of $f$” is true. Since the matrix $A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a saddle point of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite”; “$a$ is a saddle point of $f$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124570 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40d58ee6-1121-5ddc-a96f-1a7fa7a193dd" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Local Extrema Using Sylvester's Criterion"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf8f149-6cad-5a5c-9d26-11b86bcaa720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465519} {:answer/id #uuid "6b04f584-4740-59cf-8497-f747191febb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b04f584-4740-59cf-8497-f747191febb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465520} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddfefddd-b168-5878-87f2-f8f0e1876a2e" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=-19$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f9329ab-4f40-5e23-86a5-bf4d0b285377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465521} {:answer/id #uuid "5441ae78-27c1-5694-8618-d6f72b5ef496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5441ae78-27c1-5694-8618-d6f72b5ef496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465522} :answer-field/id #uuid "d143db0c-e1c0-5daa-9470-d0193838ae88" :answer-field/key "$A$ is negative-definite" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12620dec-4540-5bfc-a97c-4be11c2d223d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465523} {:answer/id #uuid "13ec6254-73f7-5076-8506-15526b0e95bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12620dec-4540-5bfc-a97c-4be11c2d223d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465523} :answer-field/id #uuid "c993b7a5-1549-5886-b715-49e5a62df038" :answer-field/key "$a$ is a local minimum of $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "175831f0-e7f9-5e35-90a3-24f7cc808fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668473} {:answer/id #uuid "da4efb78-4184-513f-b7bf-fcb1ac9798c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "175831f0-e7f9-5e35-90a3-24f7cc808fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668473} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b967bef-110d-57ea-aea5-ec9445b4f570" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00b2158a-941e-5a2f-b68c-c230bee6df19" :question/math-academy-id "q-163791" :question/problem "The quadratic Taylor approximation of the function $f(x)$ about $x=a\\in {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈8+\\frac{1}{2}(x-a)^{T}A(x-a),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $a\\in {R}^{n}$ is a critical point of the function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ if ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}.$ In such cases, we can classify $a$ as follows:\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is positive definite, then $a$ is a local minimum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is negative definite, then $a$ is a local maximum\n\n- if ${f}^{″}(a)$ is neither positive-definite nor negative-definite, then $a$ is a saddle point\n\nIn this case, we have $A={f}^{″}(a).$ Now, before we examine the statements, we recall how to categorize quadratic forms.\n\nLet ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-19$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(11)-1(-3) \\\\  & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is negative-definite” is true. Notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-2<0 \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|=7>0 \\\\ {Δ}_{3} & =|A|=-19<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the matrix $A$ is negative-definite.\n\n- Statement “$a$ is a local minimum of $f$” is false. Since the matrix $A$ is negative-definite, the critical point $a$ is a local maximum of $f.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $det(A)=-19$; “$A$ is negative-definite” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157368 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f901a3ab-3b58-51a1-b653-f88ac4b09060" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Second Derivative Test To Classify a Point on a Solution Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b05e796-e00c-5de2-9ed1-30703c297087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465531} {:answer/id #uuid "e130c91d-7b17-52a3-bbbe-7767095f3a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b05e796-e00c-5de2-9ed1-30703c297087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465531} :answer-field/id #uuid "1391c79c-130f-5328-917d-79dbf6fe63ec" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is a stationary point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea44c227-3043-5844-9d11-64a4526e8f15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465533} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1d78a3-f02f-531f-84d8-088e936f9199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea44c227-3043-5844-9d11-64a4526e8f15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465533} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a5c2786-4ef5-5ec0-8f4d-c449aa97de49" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is a local maximum point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "604a2af8-96eb-5f23-87ff-0df87135405b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465535} {:answer/id #uuid "2598aec1-6d6c-5cb8-a449-91508e4cf00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "604a2af8-96eb-5f23-87ff-0df87135405b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465535} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcee9c7c-2aa1-5f34-a629-c4b67e147f65" :answer-field/key "$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is an inflection point of the function $f$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f3e27a-71c0-597e-9a69-695c6dbcdcf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668475} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5107e0-36a0-5417-ace1-11e4ff6dba4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5107e0-36a0-5417-ace1-11e4ff6dba4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668476} :answer-field/id #uuid "822458c8-d973-5f7e-a82c-914d2bb11548" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8eeb45f2-bc46-5681-a60d-c808242e288d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164138" :question/problem "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the point $(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the first and second derivatives of the function at the given point.\n\nTo find the first derivative of $f$ at $(-\\frac{1}{2},1),$ we substitute the coordinates of our point into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1/2,1)} & ={\\left(\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right)|}_{(-1/2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the second derivative, we first need to differentiate the equation and then substitute the coordinates of the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2xy}{(1+{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2xy}{(1+{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y(1-2x)}{(1+{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\ {\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(-1/2,1)} & ={\\left(\\frac{y(1-2x)}{(1+{x}^{2})^{2}}\\right)|}_{(-1/2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1(1-2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right))}{{(1+{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is a stationary point of the function $f$” is false. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1/2,1)}=\\frac{4}{5}\\ne 0,\n$$\n\nwe obtain that $(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is not a stationary point of the function $f.$\n\n- Statement “$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is a local maximum point of the function $f$” is false. There is no critical point at $(-\\frac{1}{2},1).$ Therefore we cannot have a local minimum at that point.\n\n- Statement “$(-\\frac{1}{2},1)$ is an inflection point of the function $f$” is false. Since the second derivative is not zero, there is no inflection point at $(-\\frac{1}{2},1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfd51e38-d92a-5e3f-9610-a20858760152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465591} {:answer/id #uuid "31ed2499-deea-54d0-8415-eeb248c8c543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31ed2499-deea-54d0-8415-eeb248c8c543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b686b9cb-12bd-5580-a6e3-c47ab3efa6d0" :answer-field/key "$T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2869bddc-de10-5721-9441-0bb4e2ab4217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465593} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd2be40-511a-5bde-a15d-59a03b250eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd2be40-511a-5bde-a15d-59a03b250eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465594} :answer-field/id #uuid "54aba0a8-32f5-5c3a-8806-6ed7d2edb832" :answer-field/key "$T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b56c6ca-9473-5257-a023-177a68fb22d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465595} {:answer/id #uuid "0086d823-0762-5efc-9a6b-688329e0ad7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0086d823-0762-5efc-9a6b-688329e0ad7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465596} :answer-field/id #uuid "40045fdb-0450-5edc-9f5f-4aa6e6175f96" :answer-field/key "$T$ is a linear transformation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af3aac25-a36f-549b-ba79-65dfe1b07d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668477} {:answer/id #uuid "480d138c-41f7-5c04-9c71-fd1ff9ad5056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af3aac25-a36f-549b-ba79-65dfe1b07d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668477} :answer-field/id #uuid "00815008-634b-5f33-baaf-affa7f5c3105" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "392b472a-8eb5-510e-870b-90564b90ad03" :question/math-academy-id "q-170638" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}kx+ky \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}k(x+y) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284733 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a70e389-17f9-5e37-b90e-400709aef507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465627} {:answer/id #uuid "d59916c7-6624-57d3-9aa0-b89fb65593dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59916c7-6624-57d3-9aa0-b89fb65593dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ddd945-a9a9-5f34-9325-4506624cf8a9" :answer-field/key "$x$ is a negative number." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e7f3fb8-bf3b-5c62-a094-0338bd342f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465629} {:answer/id #uuid "106883a6-fb4f-554a-9d13-b593ed2e7a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e7f3fb8-bf3b-5c62-a094-0338bd342f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465629} :answer-field/id #uuid "52dcd415-f5ef-5cb1-80ef-962e482b89de" :answer-field/key "Why is $y$ an even number?" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d5c76a5-29e5-5b34-8ef7-febafe6faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465631} {:answer/id #uuid "585ca251-fce3-502e-8947-1413c581d399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d5c76a5-29e5-5b34-8ef7-febafe6faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a56780-9d22-5354-9ee6-e0bbeaa0aa63" :answer-field/key "${z}^{2}-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3a81177-9776-5bdb-a8e6-3affdf816e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668479} {:answer/id #uuid "368c6ef8-4f49-5de0-bf3b-a923771fe662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3a81177-9776-5bdb-a8e6-3affdf816e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668479} :answer-field/id #uuid "82bcd70b-5cba-5ece-86d1-00f07a6bba64" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d84a9618-171e-5da0-bc3f-857b9c134eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-175326" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option “$x$ is a negative number” is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “Why is $y$ an even number?” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give a question.\n\n- Option ${z}^{2}-2$ is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x$ is a negative number” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deab7354-8d59-5651-963c-4faf3b669082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465645} {:answer/id #uuid "73d28717-f191-5e1e-95bf-5af3698729dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deab7354-8d59-5651-963c-4faf3b669082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465645} :answer-field/id #uuid "decf0e43-3877-5a21-8037-cee318134af1" :answer-field/key "$P(z):$ Subtract $8$ from $z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d510c8-83d1-57f0-a77a-f71e8770f23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465647} {:answer/id #uuid "edc1cedb-d499-5519-aca9-b2bcfa1986e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8d510c8-83d1-57f0-a77a-f71e8770f23d" :answer/type {:d