fficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "388254b7-705e-581e-9708-313da2ad5c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-175342" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option “$P(z):$ Subtract $8$ from $z.$” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\n- Option “$Q(x):$ $x÷2$” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “$R(n):$ $\\sqrt{n}-\\sqrt{3}$” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a4ade3a-303a-5eec-9df3-e43d050e7127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465651} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb5336b-989f-5a31-b653-6429b31a077f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a4ade3a-303a-5eec-9df3-e43d050e7127" :answer/