of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "527ec064-c6b0-5d4a-ac97-7dea39646f9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-22495" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi , \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$”; ${f}^{″}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)<0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be22f62-445f-524d-b9e3-8e5afaa7420d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465887} {:answer/id #uuid "ebddb93c-cb3a-53b8-af7f-7c2c0137d262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2be22f62-445f-524d-b9e3-8e5afaa7420d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465887} :answer-field/id #uuid "668dee04-dff6-50da-9667-d8c73c75df22" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52e3c39d-2a51-5303-9487-acd212076b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465889} {:answer/id #uuid "38d6516f-117c-5c56-a5b5-cc594da416b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38d6516f-117c-5c56-a5b5-cc594da416b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465890} :answer-field/id #uuid "64c3d988-6f8b-5f25-b00f-eab5079bfc05" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77aecb7e-3a12-52e2-a0a0-4f675ac7f167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465891} {:answer/id #uuid "3910cc85-5508-5c6f-b6b0-d5041c8c1376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77aecb7e-3a12-52e2-a0a0-4f675ac7f167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465891} :answer-field/id #uuid "57297f62-17f1-58b7-8a9b-a5c727ad1f39" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is concave down on $(1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af9c23dc-7156-5858-a313-4e08f7251c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668513} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbe3564-75cd-5f42-9b94-c12cadf86977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af9c23dc-7156-5858-a313-4e08f7251c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668513} :answer-field/id #uuid "116f454b-c92c-53b2-ba16-3b864df8bce0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c687bf7b-334e-54f3-b20c-cd4bb1895323" :question/math-academy-id "q-22826" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x}$ defined on $x\\in (0,\\infty ).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & >0 \\\\ 2 & >\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3} & >1 \\\\ x & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that $x>0.$\n\nHence, ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ when $x>1.$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}<0,$ which has the solution $(0,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" “$f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,1)$” only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b73290-8884-52b0-bea9-586ed1106191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438082} {:answer/id #uuid "84594a5c-0472-579f-8c56-3c27f2aa0b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51b73290-8884-52b0-bea9-586ed1106191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438082} :answer-field/id #uuid "d237ec26-3cf6-575e-bb01-acccb260545f" :answer-field/key "$-3x+2=-3x+7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aa4deae-76c0-5bf7-a4af-1158715b25d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438084} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ba602a-8c17-5e28-b8db-32b4e57396a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aa4deae-76c0-5bf7-a4af-1158715b25d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438084} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0236bbe-ed0c-5681-b717-8d06a5afcad6" :answer-field/key "$6x+1=6x+5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b5cb76-d351-5058-a991-9afc4efc993e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438086} {:answer/id #uuid "b1790360-3d45-5107-959e-c1c762336309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18b5cb76-d351-5058-a991-9afc4efc993e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438086} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae99ebca-b507-5034-9f94-d990616ca1d6" :answer-field/key "$7x-4=6x-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7547f23c-0aa4-5463-8651-ed75091dbaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668515} {:answer/id #uuid "fee774d7-7c07-5356-b26d-44a89bbbf8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee774d7-7c07-5356-b26d-44a89bbbf8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668516} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e2b1594-e3d1-5c48-acb9-3b114a1a3981" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5426119-4ea0-5c84-bb6c-cf460c622db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-288425" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2 & =-3x+7 \\\\ -3x+2+3x & =-3x+7+3x \\\\ 2 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+5 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+5-6x \\\\ 1 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-4 & =6x-6 \\\\ 7x-4-6x & =6x-6-6x \\\\ x-4 & =-6 \\\\ x-4+4 & =-6+4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $7x-4=6x-6$ has the unique solution $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86bc7e66-5bdd-5da7-b6ee-6b1a37c5ae9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438088} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc3c549-6f72-5c75-9824-c4564938c74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86bc7e66-5bdd-5da7-b6ee-6b1a37c5ae9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438088} :answer-field/id #uuid "01d95513-0985-54ed-85b5-aee1f0de0676" :answer-field/key "$2x-5=x-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93091e42-4e1d-50af-874b-052e5b4ccf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438090} {:answer/id #uuid "831cc9b8-0274-570c-a213-da0beeeda4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93091e42-4e1d-50af-874b-052e5b4ccf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438090} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ccfd62c-12fc-5d4f-a40e-e4d63caedad3" :answer-field/key "$6x+1=6x+9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1844e447-1273-5f4a-9121-461fc7343eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438092} {:answer/id #uuid "fbfbb123-d421-50c5-bb94-58c01fc307f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbfbb123-d421-50c5-bb94-58c01fc307f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438093} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73ad185-931c-5fc2-9419-95cfddabcee6" :answer-field/key "$-4x+3=-4x+3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2808103a-39fd-5a55-b952-8052ebc3c17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668517} {:answer/id #uuid "39f43522-8795-541a-943e-7c3bf71b4d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2808103a-39fd-5a55-b952-8052ebc3c17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668517} :answer-field/id #uuid "e98434c4-8030-5f64-ade2-9cd2ee2f1bfb" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ef6d07-7ebc-5067-b0a5-3f361bec8d1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288427" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & =x-2 \\\\ 2x-5-x & =x-2-x \\\\ x-5 & =-2 \\\\ x-5+5 & =-2+5 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x-5=x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+1 & =6x+9 \\\\ 6x+1-6x & =6x+9-6x \\\\ 1 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3 & =-4x+3 \\\\ -4x+3+4x & =-4x+3+4x \\\\ 3 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-4x+3=-4x+3$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-4x+3=-4x+3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffdc31d0-a99c-55cb-a894-d2f460d613a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465957} {:answer/id #uuid "15e3698d-c485-5744-978c-8966c6f1e9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15e3698d-c485-5744-978c-8966c6f1e9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465958} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8e552f-3cde-5d66-b25c-bb83e47de58c" :answer-field/key "$x(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "973ba0b6-a0c4-55b7-9378-1da1968449b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465959} {:answer/id #uuid "c5bb3961-65af-5f39-842a-0a821fc0d8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "973ba0b6-a0c4-55b7-9378-1da1968449b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465959} :answer-field/id #uuid "43926316-b41f-522a-abf2-5e27e1835beb" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-t\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a63401e2-08e9-5087-9feb-36b64e7201f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465961} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf699ad-899d-510a-8ff8-487bf4b05c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a63401e2-08e9-5087-9feb-36b64e7201f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465961} :answer-field/id #uuid "4062743c-9793-5905-b74e-0d5a3e17ca24" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)⊙{x}_{2}(t)$ (element-wise product)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52980cc3-c144-529e-9ba8-fb547591bf3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668519} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed64b46-2c4d-5a16-9367-d3310f4bafa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52980cc3-c144-529e-9ba8-fb547591bf3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668519} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cb87c60-607c-59f0-8d1c-433793216b9f" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "775e3d7f-2959-5adc-b3eb-ee2a98bbde96" :question/math-academy-id "q-321646" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option $x(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-t\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier of the second term is not a constant.\n\n- Option “$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)⊙{x}_{2}(t)$ (element-wise product)” might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f6920b1-2a94-5a47-840f-c823c9f70e36" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of First-Order Linear Systems of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f74d291-c3ec-5bc4-87f6-5aa006c9ebc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465993} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5499f4-34ea-5f2a-8be2-ae18558867c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f74d291-c3ec-5bc4-87f6-5aa006c9ebc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465993} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e1421a3-ab24-57bf-8727-a502d021307f" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a65cdf03-fec5-5994-9963-81c7e656095a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465995} {:answer/id #uuid "bb95971f-6b94-559b-95a9-14b003051ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a65cdf03-fec5-5994-9963-81c7e656095a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465995} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cc1b2df-65bd-5c58-86b3-00c41699004f" :answer-field/key "$5\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b9d2e8-1e9b-52a2-bb4e-dc4e64fb5349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465997} {:answer/id #uuid "d5caddf1-dcd5-5bf4-a544-db4b20d03736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b9d2e8-1e9b-52a2-bb4e-dc4e64fb5349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465997} :answer-field/id #uuid "45c65cce-ff8e-5b99-a907-83dea3f371bc" :answer-field/key "$-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01d8b7b-312d-5010-b083-17b4c9d59a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668521} {:answer/id #uuid "9314d3d2-0388-5540-8e9f-3ee096c87fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9314d3d2-0388-5540-8e9f-3ee096c87fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668522} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d34d898-cf98-5ebb-84d9-b92ebd4ae6fa" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d50adfd6-221a-580f-9d34-b5717546927f" :question/math-academy-id "q-330300" :question/problem "Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfy the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ satisfy the inhomogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t)+f(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same inhomogeneous system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${x}_{h}(t)$ satisfies a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution to an inhomogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ then ${x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)$ is also a solution to the same inhomogeneous system.\n\nAdditonally, the *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t),…,{x}_{k}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then any linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)+⋯+{c}_{k}{x}_{k}(t)\n$$\n\nwith ${c}_{1},{c}_{2},…,{c}_{k}\\in R$ is also a solution of the same homogeneous system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expression.\n\n- Option ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that ${x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because it lacks the particular solution term ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option $5\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $5\\cdot {x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $5$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\n- Option $-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the inhomogeneous system. Notice that $-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)-{x}_{p}(t)$ can't be written as \n\n$$\n{x}_{h}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{h}(t)$ is a solution of the homogeneous system, because of the multiplier $-1$ next to the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3e49a1-1bfa-5e04-8c17-c8857487da1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466029} {:answer/id #uuid "d3353e28-5730-524e-b188-cbc30f9ff7ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f3e49a1-1bfa-5e04-8c17-c8857487da1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466029} :answer-field/id #uuid "32fa50d0-6071-515e-b834-6a08e8fef727" :answer-field/key "$x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5f51ac8-4df8-5318-b8ad-738279bb82b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466031} {:answer/id #uuid "cb88a9fa-3d2b-5935-bf50-83bed476c581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb88a9fa-3d2b-5935-bf50-83bed476c581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466032} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14d2d04-e31e-5843-867c-0f561fda2bd9" :answer-field/key "$x(t)=-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc25604f-6d66-554f-9078-a2c52836caf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466033} {:answer/id #uuid "4986099b-8e3a-58d8-b520-7af7c2ec2491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc25604f-6d66-554f-9078-a2c52836caf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466033} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e32f981-d258-539e-a80c-8c4918888146" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={e}^{2t}\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45be01fb-ea09-5aba-9a12-67a3cd6be938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668523} {:answer/id #uuid "9b938ac1-ff5f-5cb6-b834-2bb0a8aafc7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45be01fb-ea09-5aba-9a12-67a3cd6be938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668523} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a5be56f-9df2-5fad-9688-bf01d0568df4" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fac4a66c-708b-59cc-844a-c54884651cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-330332" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option $x(t)=-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$ is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=0$ and ${c}_{2}=-4,$ respectively.\n\n- Option $x(t)={e}^{2t}\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x(t)=-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95de2c3e-5810-5aa0-a1d0-b98b012572d4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Linearity Principle to the Solutions of a Homogeneous System of ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f7ae5e-83a5-5eee-b72b-dd7efc63c0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466035} {:answer/id #uuid "517876fa-dd59-539d-a674-2c1f29507c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "517876fa-dd59-539d-a674-2c1f29507c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466036} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef3ca6ba-4998-5c33-8022-e9c4136555bb" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "878ce675-1899-51cd-a7d3-a9921b8ccea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466037} {:answer/id #uuid "1f12b393-c48e-5a94-bc60-684111e47dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "878ce675-1899-51cd-a7d3-a9921b8ccea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466037} :answer-field/id #uuid "43807068-414e-57ce-9e12-5b33638cbb01" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aa9028e-ae3b-5d19-8c27-9fe05f3db2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466039} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf982e7-287d-57cb-b33a-12647e5cbc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa9028e-ae3b-5d19-8c27-9fe05f3db2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466039} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdfa6da-adb2-51cc-a641-4e5b855165cf" :answer-field/key "$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)⊙{x}_{2}(t)$ (element-wise product)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5650f113-7783-59ba-8a91-8b04fd6ecb64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668525} {:answer/id #uuid "f7069817-29e3-5397-8f8d-9b149e63fb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5650f113-7783-59ba-8a91-8b04fd6ecb64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668525} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8bbf43-13c6-5976-8660-879b6aef8145" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89894e08-2da2-5128-a91b-b1054d28b3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-330353" :question/problem "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$ might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier of the second term is not a constant.\n\n- Option “$x(t)={x}_{1}(t)⊙{x}_{2}(t)$ (element-wise product)” might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166896 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc2f3c2c-fd0f-5a5f-880a-82f786d2fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466047} {:answer/id #uuid "5eafe294-cd87-5ce6-80c3-61c5a84dab38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc2f3c2c-fd0f-5a5f-880a-82f786d2fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466047} :answer-field/id #uuid "28a05091-6793-5cc0-b4eb-1ce640b010f7" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=6{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d27ea8d-6973-5d55-8a0b-9bf18916d7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466049} {:answer/id #uuid "150d1418-d007-5c9d-a8f6-7a8d44e86905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "150d1418-d007-5c9d-a8f6-7a8d44e86905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466050} :answer-field/id #uuid "55f68aea-74bc-534e-824e-8c810de35f10" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-8{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "364859a7-aaff-5174-bdd3-5f50d200ce9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466051} {:answer/id #uuid "ce486bda-79e9-5dcc-b216-bbf4e590960e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "364859a7-aaff-5174-bdd3-5f50d200ce9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466051} :answer-field/id #uuid "4abec42a-e2c5-5ff8-8ec3-56a8bfa4ed73" :answer-field/key "$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d126c42c-030e-596c-b6db-eb3de829c1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668527} {:answer/id #uuid "45f92d87-7944-5b39-9f18-bb682e9b099a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d126c42c-030e-596c-b6db-eb3de829c1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668527} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb9bf48e-a503-55aa-a0a8-1142725e9622" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "363ad515-bb3d-517b-aff5-449014ea0698" :question/math-academy-id "q-331114" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\n{x}_{i}^{′}(t)={\\lambda }_{i}{x}_{i}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\lambda }_{i}$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=6{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-8{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-8{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on only ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$ depends on ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-8{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166896 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fde37f96-d46e-5cee-9ab6-aab431ae55be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466053} {:answer/id #uuid "2699930e-d019-57fc-8022-2330d11ba5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fde37