"false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466193} {:answer/id #uuid "da05e30d-1d4d-5bb4-85a6-726b2277403c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da05e30d-1d4d-5bb4-85a6-726b2277403c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466194} :answer-field/id #uuid "a220f624-4b00-58ea-ab26-1b0bf2dee6db" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=2.5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d51cd9b2-7a3a-5788-9485-a756a208edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466195} {:answer/id #uuid "098dc3da-4adc-5add-8a8e-89793bb8c8ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d51cd9b2-7a3a-5788-9485-a756a208edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466195} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa76ce0-7dba-57ee-b1c0-5c3c616685c6" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=3.2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "661e67d7-b640-50a2-b634-031341ceae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668551} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0129e7-dd58-57ff-a6ca-baf2e1348122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "661e67d7-b640-50a2-b634-031341ceae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668551} :answer-field/id #uuid "770c68fb-1926-56b7-84f0-d6fbd0cb3ad3" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f92808c-572e-59a4-9f7a-86aaaf0f9d81" :question/math-academy-id "q-334431" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the Runge-Kutta Method (RK4) stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the RK4 method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δ)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the RK4 Method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the RK4 Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.5)| & =|1-0.5+\\frac{(0.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(0.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(0.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{233}{384}| \\\\  & =0.606…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.5)| & =|1-1.5+\\frac{(1.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(1.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(1.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{35}{128}| \\\\  & =0.273…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(2.5)| & =|1-2.5+\\frac{(2.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(2.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(2.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{83}{128}| \\\\  & =0.648…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(3)| & =|1-3.2+\\frac{(3.2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(3.2)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(3.2)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{3427}{1875}| \\\\  & =1.827…<1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the RK4 Method is unstable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.5$; $\\lambda Δx=1.5$; $\\lambda Δx=2.5$ only.\n\nNote that the stability region of the RK4 Method is $0<\\lambda Δx<2.785…,$ so it is not absolutely stable."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5f3dbb6-3236-5c63-aae4-575fdea2d15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466213} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca860ee-7207-549a-b929-a3d3c4e8679a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ca860ee-7207-549a-b929-a3d3c4e8679a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466214} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce5ea6f3-8732-5575-b6a3-b67fb7a1d1ee" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.15$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f29f036-f1ca-52cf-97b3-96d5958e4c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466215} {:answer/id #uuid "c842b6ef-a0f1-5ab5-a956-857848597929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c842b6ef-a0f1-5ab5-a956-857848597929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466216} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21ee857-a11b-5609-a5c6-08baa0ce968d" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cc3a3e4-402c-55ad-ae38-3f8336d22a51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466217} {:answer/id #uuid "be9e186e-25fb-5dfc-b4a8-071a4b8a1ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be9e186e-25fb-5dfc-b4a8-071a4b8a1ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466218} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e593dda-1295-5d71-b1c9-dbad427fbfa3" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=2.9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b4dc7e-6ec2-5408-ae71-ff930cd18cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466219} {:answer/id #uuid "94b4c169-c254-5a0a-b54b-72a7559a691c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b4c169-c254-5a0a-b54b-72a7559a691c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466220} :answer-field/id #uuid "7983d893-d643-5aea-89b6-39f7b9e973fc" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=6.2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae88f530-077d-5e42-a7d6-ad312af736f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668553} {:answer/id #uuid "7abc6c6d-7c51-5884-9621-ae04321984dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae88f530-077d-5e42-a7d6-ad312af736f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668553} :answer-field/id #uuid "25d95f91-6bc9-5481-b780-ab3273fe3135" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ca57581-1de5-5ee9-ad10-ddff45b3ad82" :question/math-academy-id "q-334466" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the trapezoidal method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the trapezoidal method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1-\\lambda Δx/2}{1+\\lambda Δx/2}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method  ${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$ is stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\text{ }\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx)\\,{y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the trapezoidal method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1-\\lambda Δx/2}{1+\\lambda Δx/2}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the trapezoidal method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.15,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.15)| & =|\\frac{1-0.15/2}{1+0.15/2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{0.925}{1.075}| \\\\  & =0.8604…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls within the stability region, the trapezoidal method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.8)| & =|\\frac{1-0.8/2}{1+0.8/2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{0.6}{1.4}| \\\\  & =0.4285…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls within the stability region, the trapezoidal method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(2.9)| & =|\\frac{1-2.9/2}{1+2.9/2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{-0.45}{2.45}| \\\\  & =0.1836…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls within the stability region, the trapezoidal method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=6.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(6.2)| & =|\\frac{1-6.2/2}{1+6.2/2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{-2.1}{4.1}| \\\\  & =0.5121…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls within the stability region, the trapezoidal method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.15$; $\\lambda Δx=0.8$; $\\lambda Δx=2.9$; $\\lambda Δx=6.2$.\n\nNote that, since the trapezoidal method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$"}]
